  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What is the value of $f(t)=\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{2}-3),\\,\\sqrt{2t},\\,{t}^{5}\u27e9$ at $t=2?$",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=2$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({2}^{2}-3),\\sqrt{2(2)},{2}^{5}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1),\\sqrt{4},{2}^{5}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,2,32\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=2$ is the vector $\u27e80,2,32\u27e9.$",
